{"id":"f7d817d22ccbf755","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-df-singular-measures.md","title":"Singular Measure","display":"df-singular-measures — Singular Measure","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-singular-measures","aliases":["58-df-singular-measures","Singular Measure","58-df-zfc-measure11-singular-measures","58-df-zfc-measure2-singular-measures","58-df-zfc-measure9-singular-measures","58-df-zfc-measure3-mutually-singular-measures"],"display":"df-singular-measures — Singular Measure","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-singular-measures"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-singular-measures</span><span>Singular Measure</span><span>58-df-zfc-measure11-singular-measures</span><span>58-df-zfc-measure2-singular-measures</span><span>58-df-zfc-measure9-singular-measures</span><span>58-df-zfc-measure3-mutually-singular-measures</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-singular-measures — Singular Measure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu,\\nu,X,\\mathcal F\\in V\">\\(\\mu,\\nu,X,\\mathcal F\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\)</span> (measure predicate; see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MutuallySingular}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MutuallySingular}_S\\)</span> (mutual-singularity predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}measures} \\vdash \\mathrm{MutuallySingular}_S(\\mu,\\nu,X,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,X,\\mathcal F)\\land \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\nu,X,\\mathcal F)\\land \\exists A\\in\\mathcal F\\;(\\mu(A)=0\\land\\nu(X\\setminus A)=0)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}measures} \\vdash \\mathrm{MutuallySingular}_S(\\mu,\\nu,X,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,X,\\mathcal F)\\land \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\nu,X,\\mathcal F)\\land \\exists A\\in\\mathcal F\\;(\\mu(A)=0\\land\\nu(X\\setminus A)=0)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Singular: measures supported on disjoint sets</li>\n<li>Absolutely continuous: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu \\ll \\nu\">\\(\\mu \\ll \\nu\\)</span></li>\n<li>Under the standard hypotheses for Lebesgue decomposition, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu=\\mu_{ac}+\\mu_s\">\\(\\mu=\\mu_{ac}+\\mu_s\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu_s\\perp\\nu\">\\(\\mu_s\\perp\\nu\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The Cantor distribution is singular with respect to Lebesgue measure.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rudin, Real and Complex Analysis</li>\n<li>Billingsley, Probability and Measure</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Measure}_S$ (measure predicate; see [[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mu,\\nu,X,\\mathcal F\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MutuallySingular}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}measures} \\vdash \\mathrm{MutuallySingular}_S(\\mu,\\nu,X,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,X,\\mathcal F)\\land \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\nu,X,\\mathcal F)\\land \\exists A\\in\\mathcal F\\;(\\mu(A)=0\\land\\nu(X\\setminus A)=0)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mu \\ll \\nu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu=\\mu_{ac}+\\mu_s","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu_s\\perp\\nu","display":false}],"bytes":1343,"backlinks":[{"id":"2ab9485c68bf8ab2","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"f3ad34116c96ab00","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1178","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-singular-measures.md|58-df-singular-measures]]（batch01）"}],"outgoing":["ca832ed6bc22f728"]}